---
source: crates/mcp/tests/it/listing.rs
expression: info.instructions.clone().unwrap_or_default()
---
devlanes runs a dev environment per Git worktree (a lane) with its own ports, URLs and env. This server only reads: ask the user to start, stop or change anything. Common commands have tools of their own; the devlanes tool runs the others that change nothing.
- wait blocks until ready or failed: no sleep or curl polling.
- Read a unit with `logs {"units": ["web"], "tail": 100}`, the lane with status, a failure with `debug_why {"unit": "web"}`, CPU and memory with debug_top, setup problems with doctor.
- cwd picks the worktree; without it the call uses the project the agent runs in.
